{# SKILL.md scaffold for a loomv2 `type: workflow` skill.

   Render with the template skill, adding this folder and
   ~/.kiro/skills/home/loomv2/templates as --include-dir so the
   loomv2 host partials resolve.

   Variables:
     name, description  — frontmatter (description carries triggers)
     title              — H1
     intro              — 1-3 sentences
     prefix             — shell prefix, e.g. "PD"
     shim               — always "LOOM" (loomv2 partials read it)
     skill_name         — kebab name for tiling labels
     location           — namespace under ~/.kiro/skills/, e.g. "home"
     target             — tiling label placeholder, e.g. "<op>"
     dependencies       — markdown bullets
     parameters         — markdown bullets
     caller_vars        — bash lines setting caller state (e.g. PD_OP=...)
     graph_arg          — e.g. '--graph "graph-$PD_OP.yaml"' or ""
     set_assignments    — entry seeds, e.g. '--set name="$PD_NAME"'
     rules              — numbered list (skill-specific; the inline
                          dispatch rule is always rule 1)
     completion         — table body rows, one per status
     plan_visualisation — "" or non-empty to link
                          references/plan-topology.md
     references         — "" or markdown bullets linking references/*.md
#}
