## Rules

1. A `ready` batch with exactly one agent task MAY run inline: read its
   `prompt_path`, follow it, write the output, then `runtime complete`.
   Two or more agent tasks MUST go to parallel sub-agents.
2. Human gates MUST be driven by the user; never auto-complete them.
3. A failed task aborts the run; report BLOCKED with `error_path`, do not
   re-run it.
{{ rules }}

## Workflow

### Step 1: Ingest

1. Set tiling activity:
   ```bash
   {{ prefix }}_TILING=~/.kiro/skills/home/tiling/scripts/run-ttm.sh
   ${{ prefix }}_TILING activity set "{{ skill_name }}({{ target }}): Ingest"
   ```
2. Set up aliases, caller state, and the tiling layout:
   ```bash
   {{ prefix }}_SKILLS=~/.kiro/skills
   {{ prefix }}_ROOT=${{ prefix }}_SKILLS/{{ location }}/{{ skill_name }}
   {{ prefix }}_{{ shim }}=${{ prefix }}_SKILLS/home/loomv2/scripts/loom.sh
   {{ prefix }}_EDITOR=${{ prefix }}_SKILLS/home/editor/scripts/run-editor.sh
{{ caller_vars | indent(3, first=True) }}
   eval "$(${{ prefix }}_TILING layout build)"
   ```
3. Init the run (auto workdir under `/tmp/{{ skill_name }}/`):
   ```bash
   {{ prefix }}_WD=$(${{ prefix }}_{{ shim }} runtime init \
       --loom-root "${{ prefix }}_ROOT/loom"{% if graph_arg %} {{ graph_arg }}{% endif %} \
       {{ set_assignments }})
   ```
4. If `runtime init` fails: NEEDS_CONTEXT. On success: proceed to Step 2.

